To issue a Stripe refund, you would typically use the Stripe API's refund endpoint. Here's a basic example of how you might do this using the Stripe Node.js library:

```javascript
const stripe = require('stripe')('YOUR_STRIPE_SECRET_KEY');

stripe.refunds.create({
  charge: 'CHARGE_ID',
  amount: 100, // Amount in cents
  reason: 'customer_refund',
  description: 'Refund for customer'
}, (err, refund) => {
  if (err) {
    console.error(err);
  } else {
    console.log(refund);
  }
});
```

Replace `'YOUR_STRIPE_SECRET_KEY'` with your actual Stripe secret key and `'CHARGE_ID'` with the ID of the charge you want to refund. This code will create a refund for the specified charge, reducing the balance of the customer's account by the specified amount.
